+# Task Report: CORE-003 — Equipment Audit Model & Synthetic Mock Bill Generator
+
+**Date:** 2026-10-19  
+**Agent:** gemini  
+**Task ID:** CORE-003 (covers CORE-003.1 – CORE-003.4)  
+**Status:** done  
+**Patch File:** `patch/CORE-003-gemini-equipment-mock-bills.patch`  
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+This task implemented the complete equipment audit domain model, CSV schemas, concrete CCIS 18-room inventory fixture, and calibrated synthetic monthly electricity bill generator for the **MMSU College of Computing and Information Sciences (CCIS)** facility (~2,500 m²).
+
+Key achievements delivered:
+1. **Equipment Audit Schema & Fixture (`CORE-003.1`, `CORE-003.2`):**
+   - Established `data/fixtures/equipment-audit-schema.csv` specifying `item, room_type, count, rated_kw, hours_per_day, tier, duty_cycle, notes`.
+   - Created `data/fixtures/equipment-audit-ccis.csv` parameterizing all 18 dedicated rooms from decision **[D-06]** (6 computer labs, 6 lecture halls, 2 hyflex smart classrooms, 1 Dean + Secretary suite, 1 COD office, 2 faculty rooms, plus building infrastructure).
+   - Classified all 38 equipment lines into the three priority tiers locked in **[D-10]** (Tier 1 life safety: 1.21 kW / ~1% connected / ~1.5% peak; Tier 2 operational continuity: 17.5 kW / ~12% connected / ~17% peak; Tier 3 comfort cooling & sheddable labs: 121.3 kW / ~87% connected / ~81% peak; Total connected load = 140.01 kW).
+2. **Domain Model & Loader (`src/ccis_sim/demand/equipment.py`):**
+   - Implemented immutable `EquipmentItem` and `EquipmentAudit` dataclasses with physical bounds validation, tier and room aggregation, and direct compatibility with CORE-001's `Building` and `RoomInventory` dataclasses.
+3. **Synthetic Monthly Bill Generator (`CORE-003.3`, `src/ccis_sim/demand/mock_bills.py`):**
+   - Implemented `SyntheticBillGenerator` and `SyntheticMonthlyBill` incorporating academic semester weighting (SUC academic timetable), Batac seasonal cooling degree multipliers (0.85–1.25), 10% nighttime standby baseload (8.0 kW per DEM-001.3), and Gaussian meter noise ($\sigma = 2.5\%$).
+   - Explicitly marked all outputs with `is_synthetic = True` and `data_origin = "SYNTHETIC_MOCK_CALIBRATED_AUDIT"`, fulfilling decision **[D-03]**'s constraint to avoid unlabelled mock data.
+   - Committed the calibrated 12-month baseline fixture at `data/fixtures/synthetic-mock-bills-ccis.csv`.
+4. **Plausibility Validation Against Regional EUI Benchmark (`CORE-003.4`):**
+   - Implied Annual Electricity Consumption: **398,536.77 kWh/year**.
+   - Implied Annual Energy Use Intensity (EUI): **159.41 kWh/m²·yr**.
+   - Conformance: Strictly within the regional academic benchmark band of **150.0 – 300.0 kWh/m²·yr** locked in `status.md`.
+   - Automated conformance assertion verified via pytest.
+5. **Architectural Decisions Logged:**
+   - Formalized and appended decision **[D-16]** in `docs/decisions/decision-log.md`.
+
