+
+### 2.2 Alignment with Architectural Decisions
+
+- **[D-03] (Zero Institutional Data Requests):**
+  - No MMSU utility bills were requested. The model relies entirely on a self-conducted bottom-up equipment audit and a synthetic monthly bill generator calibrated against engineering principles and regional benchmarks.
+- **[D-06] (CCIS 18-Room Facility Layout):**
+  - The audit accounts for all 18 dedicated rooms: 6 computer labs, 6 lecture halls, 2 hyflex smart classrooms, 1 Dean + Secretary suite, 1 COD office, and 2 faculty rooms, plus distributed IDF networking closets and common corridors.
+  - Floor area reconciles exactly with `2,500.0 m²` from `Building.gross_floor_area_m2`.
+- **[D-10] (Priority-Based Critical Load Classification):**
+  - Tier 1 (Life safety): 1.21 kW connected (~0.9% connected, ~1.5% peak), operating 24/7 (exit signs, stairwell lighting, fire alarm, CCTV).
+  - Tier 2 (Operational continuity): 17.5 kW connected (~12.5% connected, ~17% peak), including distributed IDF switches, telecommunication closet spot-cooling, Dean/COD offices, faculty terminals, and water pump.
+  - Tier 3 (Comfort cooling & sheddable loads): 121.3 kW connected (~86.6% connected, ~81% peak), including student workstations, lecture room ACs, lab ACs, and comfort lighting, shed immediately upon utility outages.
+- **[D-16] (Equipment Audit Inventory & Synthetic Billing Calibration Baseline):**
+  - Parameterized equipment counts and ratings based on actual Philippine state university operational standards (e.g. 40 workstations at 180 W per lab, dual 3.0 HP inverter split AC units per lab to handle internal thermal heat dissipation in Batac's tropical climate).
